{"name":"Crocodile Tears","hex":"#d6d69b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crocodile tears","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of crocodile tear"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodile_tears"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocodile Tears (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Crocodile Tears is a 2024 coming-of-age thriller film directed and written by Tumpal Tampubolon in his directorial debut. It stars Yusuf Mahardika, Zulfa Maharani, and Marissa Anita."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ef/Air_mata_buaya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile_Tears_(film)"},{"title":"Alex Rider (book series)","blocks":[{"text":"Alex Rider is a series of spy novels by the English author Anthony Horowitz. The novels revolve around the teenaged spy Alex Rider and are primarily aimed towards young adults. The series comprises 14 novels, as well as seven graphic novels, seven short stories, and a supplementary book."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Stormbreakerbook.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_Rider_(book_series)"},{"title":"Crocodile tears","blocks":[{"text":"Crocodile tears, or superficial sympathy, is a colloquial term used to describe a false, insincere display of emotion, such as a hypocrite crying fake tears of grief. The phrase derives from an ancient belief that crocodiles shed tears while consuming their prey and, as such, is present in many modern languages, especially in Europe, where it was introduced through Latin. While crocodiles do have tear ducts, they weep to lubricate their eyes, typically when they have been out of water for a long time and their eyes begin to dry out. However, evidence suggests this could also be triggered by feeding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Grant%27s_crocodile_tears.jpg/330px-Grant%27s_crocodile_tears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile_tears"},{"title":"Crocodile","blocks":[{"text":"A crocodile or true crocodile is a large, semiaquatic reptile that lives throughout the tropics in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Australia. The term \"crocodile\" is sometimes used more loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes the alligators and caimans, the gharial and false gharial as well as other extinct taxa. This article uses \"crocodile\" or \"true crocodile\" to refer only to the species taxonomically included in the Crocodylidae family, extant or extinct."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/330px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png/500px-Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png/1280px-Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png/500px-Crocodile_tears_for_Syria.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Crocodile tears for Syria\", cartoon by Carlos Latuff illustrating the concept","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrocodile_tears_for_Syria.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Crocodylus_porosus_-_Eye_-_Wilhelma.jpg/500px-Crocodylus_porosus_-_Eye_-_Wilhelma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, h